        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21246809?u=3732e82281d416b384d21367407282a84f52640b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In the HTTP header glossary page there are two HTTP response examples, but they are missing the HTTP version. This commit adds the version to produce a correct HTTP response message.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Since MDN is read not only by professionals but also by people who are just starting to learn how HTTP works, it may be better to be more precise when writing an example HTTP response.</p>",
