        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Remove <code class=\"notranslate\">Cookie2</code> from a list, reverting its addition in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3597714135\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41830\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41830/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41830\">#41830</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">Cookie2</code> was originally removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1171605947\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/13965\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/13965/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/13965\">#13965</a> because the header is not supported by any browser - where supported means \"the browser actually does something to include it\", not that it can be included by servers etc.<br>\nWhile we'd happily include something that has no browser integration, we don't include headers that are obsoleted and have no browser integration, because they are no longer considered part of the web platform,</p>",
